Syntax: bolster <item>

Bolster works a piece of armor up toward the most it could ever be, spending
soulstone charges to do it.

There is no set length.  It runs until the piece reaches its ceiling, until
the stone runs dry, or until something stops you.  The ceiling is the tier's
own maximum, opening fully at level thirty-five, so heavy armor can reach
fifty-five and clothing something well short of that.

Every attempt costs charges whether it lands or not, and the cost rises with
the piece: a fine piece is dear to improve and a plain one is cheap.  A
better stone pays a tenth of what a poor one pays for the same work.

The difficulty is read fresh each attempt from how far along the piece
already is, so the last stretch of a heavy piece is the hardest work in the
game, and monk's clothing is comparatively easy to finish.

